  "findings": [
    "Both actual held-destination reader routes succeed with one original locked writer call, one replacement attempt, one returned Ex22 rename, source fd closed before replacement, and both native handles closed.",
    "The original process-controller assertions verify the held reader sees its old snapshot and the new destination path sees the new contents; no raw token/path content is exported by the child report.",
    "Both independently held source-CRT cases fail at source_open with PermissionError/errno13/WinError32 before any Ex22 rename call; reader and source holder cleanup completes.",
    "An independently held destination-CRT reader without delete sharing still rejects the one Ex22 rename with WinError32; readonly and directory destinations reject with WinError5.",
    "Unheld and missing destinations succeed. No retry, fallback, readonly-ignore flag or permission widening was added.",
    "The observed audit mode records the same single original os.rename arguments before native opens; refusal preserves the exact original exception object with zero native opens/renames.",
    "Wrong source identity, directory source and reparse source guards reject before mutation and leave no owned handle. The extra ABI/name-buffer test constructs and checks the argument buffer but does not itself call the API.",
    "Separate synthetic controls preserve source-descriptor cleanup on snapshot failure and distinguish committed rename from later CloseHandle failure.",
    "All thirteen child capture bodies match their recorded byte lengths, SHA256 and parsed report properties; every direct child retired without timeout, kill, transport error, stderr or cleanup error."
  ],
