  "limits": [
    "This is a successful isolated source-level API mechanism experiment on the retained Windows runner, not an implemented or installed product writer.",
    "The helper is reached through the declared CI-only writer facade probe. A coherent product reader/writer implementation and permanent normal-Windows test selection are still required.",
    "Current Microsoft documentation permits both relative-root and absolute-name forms. This result establishes the tested argument-form distinction on this runner, not a universal explanation of the prior87.",
    "Full-path destination resolution is not anchored through the held parent handle; no all-ancestor namespace or every-filesystem guarantee is established.",
    "The separate WTEXT preservation gate stopped at typing errors; Unicode acceptance remains unexecuted here.",
    "Python executable identity is runner-recorded and unchanged before/after; its binary and the ZIP binary are not included in the Git evidence tree.",
